WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.901
-You have
a very exciting role coming up.

00:00:01.901 --> 00:00:02.836 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I do, yes.

00:00:02.836 --> 00:00:04.904 line:92%
-This is a Unabomber TV movie?

00:00:04.904 --> 00:00:08.375 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right. This is Discovery's
first scripted series,

00:00:08.375 --> 00:00:09.209 line:92%
and it's about the Unabomber.

00:00:09.209 --> 00:00:11.945
And it's with Paul Bettany
and Chris Noth, and I play --

00:00:11.945 --> 00:00:12.612 size:75% position:38% line:92%
and Sam Worthington.

00:00:12.612 --> 00:00:14.881 size:81% position:41%
And I play Janet Reno,
the attorney general.

00:00:14.881 --> 00:00:16.516 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Janet Reno.
-Yes.

00:00:16.516 --> 00:00:20.020 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I mean, it's kind of nuts
how good that is.

00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:22.822 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, there's always the risk
of looking like

00:00:22.822 --> 00:00:26.760
a terrible wig and glasses,
which I don't think I do.

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:27.327 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Well, that --

00:00:27.327 --> 00:00:30.096 size:78% position:39%
I would say that risk
would be this, right?

00:00:30.096 --> 00:00:30.630 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-There we go.

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:32.565 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That would be the risk
of a terrible wig and glasses.

00:00:32.565 --> 00:00:34.434 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:34.434 --> 00:00:36.503
-Actually, he was my jumping-off
point for this character.

00:00:36.503 --> 00:00:37.904 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That was
your jumping off point?

00:00:37.904 --> 00:00:38.872 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Absolutely, yes.
-Yeah.

00:00:38.872 --> 00:00:39.906 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But I was a big fan
of Janet Reno,

00:00:39.906 --> 00:00:41.741
and, boy, we could use somebody
like her today, couldn't we?

00:00:41.741 --> 00:00:42.409 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-Yeah, that's great.

00:00:42.409 --> 00:00:44.277
And was it fun --
Did you get to meet her at all?

00:00:44.277 --> 00:00:45.678 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I didn't.
No, in fact, she passed away

00:00:45.678 --> 00:00:47.447
right before we started doing --
started shooting.

00:00:47.447 --> 00:00:48.148 line:92%
-Oh, well that's too bad.

00:00:48.148 --> 00:00:51.051
-Yeah, but I did speak to a guy
who was her assistant.

00:00:51.051 --> 00:00:53.653 align:start size:94% position:6%
Now he's, like, my age,
but he knew her very well,

00:00:53.653 --> 00:00:56.489 size:88% position:44%
and, gosh, he just told
great stories about her.

00:00:56.489 --> 00:00:57.424 line:92%
She had such a huge heart.

00:00:57.424 --> 00:00:59.926 align:start size:94% position:6%
She had a lot of big cases
on her desk,

00:00:59.926 --> 00:01:01.127 line:92%
not just the Unabomber case,

00:01:01.127 --> 00:01:03.797 align:start size:94% position:6%
but Waco, and Whitewater,
and the whole thing.

00:01:03.797 --> 00:01:05.532 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it was --
it was a tough time,

00:01:05.532 --> 00:01:08.068 align:start size:94% position:6%
but we were lucky to have her
in that office.

00:01:08.068 --> 00:01:09.903 size:78% position:39%
-It's also kind of --
I mean, this isn't --

00:01:09.903 --> 00:01:12.205 align:start size:94% position:6%
This sounds like a weird thing
to say, but it is --

00:01:12.205 --> 00:01:14.274
Sometimes with everything crazy
going on today,

00:01:14.274 --> 00:01:16.109 align:start size:94% position:6%
you forget that there were
crazy things happening

00:01:16.109 --> 00:01:16.776 size:78% position:39% line:92%
in the '90s, as well.

00:01:16.776 --> 00:01:19.379
-Yeah, there was, but it seemed
like they were adults.

00:01:19.379 --> 00:01:20.580 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, that's true.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:23.450 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It seemed like --
You know, you had Janet Reno,

00:01:23.450 --> 00:01:26.553 align:start size:94% position:6%
who had such independence
from the president,

00:01:26.553 --> 00:01:27.620 line:92%
and, you know, is the one

00:01:27.620 --> 00:01:29.422 align:start size:94% position:6%
who appointed
the special prosecutor

00:01:29.422 --> 00:01:33.126
for Whitewater, and, you know,
that was just -- I don't know.

00:01:33.126 --> 00:01:36.029 size:81% position:41%
I'm, like, sentimental
for the '90s, I guess.

00:01:36.029 --> 00:01:36.596 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I don't know.

00:01:36.596 --> 00:01:39.499
But it just seemed like
there was some integrity.

00:01:39.499 --> 00:01:41.634 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You played Janet Reno
on stage before.

00:01:41.634 --> 00:01:43.636 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, I did.
-And what was that production?

00:01:43.636 --> 00:01:46.739 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That was called "Baby Jesus
and His Holiday Pixies."

00:01:46.739 --> 00:01:48.007 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, is this maybe --
-Yes.

00:01:48.007 --> 00:01:50.110 align:start size:94% position:6%
-This also had
a great amount of integrity.

00:01:50.110 --> 00:01:51.845 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Indeed.
Oh, of course, yes.

00:01:51.845 --> 00:01:52.946 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Where was this?
Where did you do this?

00:01:52.946 --> 00:01:56.182
-This was in Los Angeles,
at the Tamarind Theatre,

00:01:56.182 --> 00:01:57.450 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
which is now UCB.

00:01:57.450 --> 00:02:00.587
I did "Run, Run Rudolph"
with little baby Jesuses.

00:02:00.587 --> 00:02:01.254 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, wow.
-Yeah.

00:02:01.254 --> 00:02:03.656 align:start size:94% position:6%
-As Janet Reno?
-As Janet Reno, yes.

00:02:03.656 --> 00:02:04.290 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-That's fantastic.

00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:06.993 align:start size:94% position:6%
Now, I know you travel light,
but this is obviously

00:02:06.993 --> 00:02:08.328 align:start size:94% position:6%
just coming over for the day.
-Yes.

00:02:08.328 --> 00:02:10.630 align:start size:94% position:6%
-When you travel,
when you get on an airplane,

00:02:10.630 --> 00:02:11.531 line:92%
you obviously have more stuff,

00:02:11.531 --> 00:02:13.399
and I heard you had a bit
of a luggage incident.

00:02:13.399 --> 00:02:16.035 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I did. Yeah, well I always do
the carry-on thing.

00:02:16.035 --> 00:02:18.037 align:start size:94% position:6%
-As you should.
You got to travel light.

00:02:18.037 --> 00:02:18.605 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes, exactly.

00:02:18.605 --> 00:02:21.608
And I was coming back
from Provincetown Film Festival,

00:02:21.608 --> 00:02:22.542 line:92%
and I won an award there.

00:02:22.542 --> 00:02:24.410 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Congratulations.
-Thank you so much!

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:26.479 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Cheers and applause ]
Hey, thanks!

00:02:26.479 --> 00:02:29.282 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it went through the X-ray,
and they pulled me aside,

00:02:29.282 --> 00:02:32.852
and they said, "Ma'am, do you
have something in your suitcase

00:02:32.852 --> 00:02:34.220 line:92%
you want to tell me about?"

00:02:34.220 --> 00:02:36.689 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I said,
"No. Well, what did you see?"

00:02:36.689 --> 00:02:41.060
So, we saw something,
and it's shaped like a cylinder.

00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:41.828 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And I went, "What?"

00:02:41.828 --> 00:02:43.563 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he said,
"And if you don't remember,

00:02:43.563 --> 00:02:46.566
and you can't tell me right now
what it is,

00:02:46.566 --> 00:02:48.001 line:92%
you're going into that room,

00:02:48.001 --> 00:02:50.670 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we're taking your bag
into that room."

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:52.539 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I remembered
it was the award.

00:02:52.539 --> 00:02:53.406 line:92%
They thought it was a pipe bomb.

00:02:53.406 --> 00:02:55.241 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's long, it's skinny.
-Oh, my goodness.

00:02:55.241 --> 00:02:55.875 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-Yes, so that was --

00:02:55.875 --> 00:02:57.911 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, it's a good thing
they're watching.

00:02:57.911 --> 00:02:58.678 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Yeah, you know.

00:02:58.678 --> 00:03:00.847 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And they're like,
"Also, we noticed you have

00:03:00.847 --> 00:03:01.814 line:92%
a script for the Unabomber."

00:03:01.814 --> 00:03:05.084 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, right, exactly!
[ Laughter ]

00:03:05.084 --> 00:03:05.818 size:78% position:39% line:92%
"What's up with you?"

00:03:05.818 --> 00:03:07.487 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"And so we have
a lot of issues here.

00:03:07.487 --> 00:03:09.856 align:start size:94% position:6%
We're not great
at connecting the dots,

00:03:09.856 --> 00:03:12.792
but you're making it very easy."
-Yes, yes.

00:03:12.792 --> 00:03:13.326 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-We first met --

00:03:13.326 --> 00:03:15.295 align:start size:94% position:6%
I guess it was 2010
when you hosted "SNL."

00:03:15.295 --> 00:03:16.196 line:92%
-Yes, when I did "SNL," yeah.

00:03:16.196 --> 00:03:17.864 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And it was really great,
because it was you,

00:03:17.864 --> 00:03:18.698 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
it was Bruno Mars.

00:03:18.698 --> 00:03:19.499 line:92%
That his first time on the show.

00:03:19.499 --> 00:03:21.668
-That was his first time.
And I'll tell you what, though.

00:03:21.668 --> 00:03:23.803 align:start size:94% position:6%
The way you guys
work over there,

00:03:23.803 --> 00:03:24.837 line:92%
I thought it was going to be,

00:03:24.837 --> 00:03:27.006 align:start size:94% position:6%
we rehearse the same scenes
all week long,

00:03:27.006 --> 00:03:29.075 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then we're perfected
for Friday --

00:03:29.075 --> 00:03:30.009 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
or, Saturday night.

00:03:30.009 --> 00:03:31.477 align:start size:94% position:6%
Friday...
Saturday night.

00:03:31.477 --> 00:03:34.480 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we changed stuff
every two se--

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:36.516 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Right before the show.

00:03:36.516 --> 00:03:37.250 size:78% position:39% line:92%
I didn't even have --

00:03:37.250 --> 00:03:39.085
You were the head writer,
and you were supposed to be

00:03:39.085 --> 00:03:39.819 size:84% position:42% line:92%
giving me my monologue.

00:03:39.819 --> 00:03:41.621 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I kept going,
"When's Seth coming?

00:03:41.621 --> 00:03:42.422 size:75% position:38% line:92%
When's Seth coming?"

00:03:42.422 --> 00:03:43.556 line:92%
And then, like, the day before,

00:03:43.556 --> 00:03:45.458 align:start size:94% position:6%
you said,
"Oh, we're gonna do a song."

00:03:45.458 --> 00:03:46.793 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-[ Sighs ] "Okay."

00:03:46.793 --> 00:03:48.561 size:81% position:41%
But it was really fun.
I really enjoyed it.

00:03:48.561 --> 00:03:50.296 align:start size:94% position:6%
-By the way,
I feel terrible for you

00:03:50.296 --> 00:03:51.965 align:start size:94% position:6%
that, like,
Bruno Mars was there

00:03:51.965 --> 00:03:52.999 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you had me
writing you a song.

00:03:52.999 --> 00:03:54.767
-[ Laughing ]
It was really a fantastic song!

00:03:54.767 --> 00:03:55.969 size:88% position:44%
-Okay, good, good, good!
I'm glad you liked it.

00:03:55.969 --> 00:03:58.238 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It had Fred Armisen in it.
It was great.

00:03:58.238 --> 00:04:00.139 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, it was
such a lovely week.

00:04:00.139 --> 00:04:00.607 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-It was.

00:04:00.607 --> 00:04:02.475 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And it's, in general, just
great to see you always, Jane.

00:04:04.377 --> 00:04:05.378 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Congratulations.
So happy the show is back.

00:04:05.378 --> 00:04:06.980 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, thank you.
I'm happy for you.

00:04:06.980 --> 00:04:08.948 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you.
Jane Lynch, everybody!

00:04:08.948 --> 00:04:11.017 size:81% position:41%
"Hollywood Game Night"
airs Thursday nights

00:04:11.017 --> 00:04:12.652 size:75% position:38% line:92%
at 8:00 p.m. on NBC!

